Most television reception difficulties are caused by problems with antennas, equipment or installation, and can often be easily resolved.
General Troubleshooting Tips
Check if the problem occurs on all channels or just one
Check all the cables are connected correctly and not loose
Try replacing the cable connecting your external antenna wall socket and your TV
Try another TV in the same location (if available) to check if its specific to that TV
Restore the default settings and "rescan" on your television or set top box
Remove/disconnect all other equipment (VCRS, PVRS, pay-tv boxes and surround sound systems) and see if the problem still occurs
Move radios or computer equipment away from the TV
Check your antenna has not moved or been broken (damage on one small part can cause the loss of a single channel). Read more about antennas.
Turn off nearby electrical appliances and see if the problems cease
Check with your neighbours - if they aren't having the same problem it's something in your house or your antenna
Check to see if there is any maintenance work happening on the ABC transmitters for your area
