If you have been into a bookmakers in the recent past then you will have seen fixed-odds betting terminals (FOBT), lining the walls and probably attracting plenty of custom.
These are the gaming machines that allow customers to play a range of games including poker, blackjack, simulated horse racing, and most popular of all, roulette.
They are called FOBTs simply because the games played on them pay out at fixed odds.
You will also see FOBTs in casinos and at racetracks as well, but most can be found in the bookies, with each betting shop allowed no more than four on their premises but over 34,000 of them now across the UK.
(Picture: Daniel Hambury/PA Wire)
There are two categories of these machine in operation at the moment; the B3 games which have a maximum stake of £2 and a maximum prize of £500.
Then there are the B2 games in which you can place a £100 stake, but can still only win £500 (your chances of winning are increased by the vastly increased stake).
The £100 maximum stake is per spin, which can be as regular as every 20 seconds, which means gamblers can lose £300-per-minute if their luck is out.
