Whilst fruit machines have been visible as a form of gaming machines in pubs for many years, their relatively low stake and low return makes them less of an issue.
The potential for immediate big wins on FOBTs in bookmakers have made them a very dangerous prospect for gambling addicts and a very profitable endeavour for the bookies.
FOBTs generated over £1.8bn in revenue for bookmakers in 2016, and, as a result, have been labelled the ��crack cocaine of gambling.��
